00:57:41,585 --> 00:57:45,389
It's an honor to meet you all

985
00:57:45,389 --> 00:57:49,493
and be part of X THE LEAGUE.

986
00:57:49,493 --> 00:57:51,528
I look forward to seeing you grow,

987
00:57:51,528 --> 00:57:54,164
build amazing futures,
and enjoy your brightest moments.

988
00:57:54,164 --> 00:57:56,224
I'm BamBam. Thank you.

989
00:57:59,139 --> 00:58:01,572
[EHCO, EPEX]

990
00:58:02,239 --> 00:58:05,676
[EPEX takes the stage to keep the energy high]

991
00:58:14,902 --> 00:58:18,892
[EPEX turns the excitement up another notch]

992
00:58:30,834 --> 00:58:34,138
[Pookie, FIFTY FIFTY]

993
00:58:45,949 --> 00:58:46,950
Let's go.

994
00:58:46,950 --> 00:58:50,667
[Filling the ceremony
with sweet, upbeat energy]

995
00:58:55,392 --> 00:58:57,995
[FIFTY FIFTY's finale leaves a lasting buzz]

996
00:58:59,196 --> 00:59:01,899
Why don't we take a moment

997
00:59:01,899 --> 00:59:05,901
to chat with our sellers and cast?

998
00:59:05,901 --> 00:59:08,405
I'd like to ask Team Korea a question.

999
00:59:08,405 --> 00:59:10,340
As we wrap up the league,

1000
00:59:10,340 --> 00:59:16,213
which mission stands out as the toughest?

1001
00:59:16,213 --> 00:59:19,283
Honestly, none of the missions were difficult.

1002
00:59:19,283 --> 00:59:26,457
But I don't usually do livestreams,
so that part was a little tough.

1003
00:59:26,457 --> 00:59:29,960
- Livestreaming seems to be hard for everyone.
- That's right.

1004
00:59:29,960 --> 00:59:32,896
If you had another chance,
would you do it again?

1005
00:59:32,896 --> 00:59:35,032
I'll let someone else have a turn.

1006
00:59:35,032 --> 00:59:36,233
It must have been really tough.

1007
00:59:36,233 --> 00:59:37,668
It was tough, but I gave it my best.

1008
00:59:37,668 --> 00:59:40,471
- So you have no regrets.
- No regrets.

1009
00:59:40,471 --> 00:59:42,773
- You gave it everything.
- Absolutely.

1010
00:59:42,773 --> 00:59:47,744
Next, a question for Team SG&MY.

1011
00:59:47,744 --> 00:59:49,880
Where are you? There you are, right up front.

1012
00:59:49,880 --> 00:59:52,749
[We're right here]
- You're in good spirits. - Yes, they are.

1013
00:59:52,749 --> 00:59:57,459
What Korean phrase did you pick up most
on X THE LEAGUE?

1014
00:59:58,021 --> 00:59:59,880
"Yes, understood."

1015
01:00:01,291 --> 01:00:03,293
- She sounds just like someone...
- This is...

1016
01:00:03,293 --> 01:00:04,934
- in Korean broadcasting...
- Like a Korean office worker.

1017
01:00:04,934 --> 01:00:07,501
Exactly. That means they're
feeling pretty tense right now.

1018
01:00:07,501 --> 01:00:09,533
[Korean office worker mode: stiff and formal]
Exactly. Even our sellers have picked up

1019
01:00:09,533 --> 01:00:11,868
the Korean office worker mindset.

1020
01:00:11,868 --> 01:00:14,701
How did you end up learning that phrase?

1021
01:00:14,701 --> 01:00:18,108
Where did you hear it?

1022
01:00:18,108 --> 01:00:20,744
Sonia did a lot of interpreting for us.

1023
01:00:20,744 --> 01:00:26,987
"Yes, understood" was a response
I could easily learn.

1024
01:00:26,987 --> 01:00:28,934
[Awkward]
That's a different mindset from ours.

1025
01:00:28,934 --> 01:00:31,659
- She was just being open-minded.
- She's a positive person.

1026
01:00:31,659 --> 01:00:34,034
We were thinking in terms of obedience.

1027
01:00:34,034 --> 01:00:35,067
That's right.

1028
01:00:35,067 --> 01:00:37,200
Now it's time for the real finale.

1029
01:00:37,200 --> 01:00:40,330
- Yes, the real finale.
- X THE LEAGUE The Final Celebration.

1030
01:00:40,330 --> 01:00:43,066
We have just one award left.

1031
01:00:43,066 --> 01:00:46,136
At last, the overall winner

1032
01:00:46,136 --> 01:00:48,272
- will be revealed.
- Yes, right now.

1033
01:00:48,272 --> 01:00:52,200
[Korea & Indonesia secure the top 2 spots]

1034
01:00:52,200 --> 01:00:54,444
First, let's applaud all the sellers

1035
01:00:54,444 --> 01:00:58,081
who worked so hard
throughout this long journey.

1036
01:00:58,081 --> 01:01:01,785
[Thank you to every seller who joined us]

1037
01:01:01,785 --> 01:01:04,934
It's time to reveal which country's team

1038
01:01:04,934 --> 01:01:09,346
will take home the $500,000 grand prize.

1039
01:01:09,960 --> 01:01:12,267
The two countries that made it to the end

1040
01:01:12,267 --> 01:01:16,867
will now face off to become
the first-ever X THE LEAGUE champion.

1041
01:01:16,867 --> 01:01:18,335
[Only Korea & Indonesia remain
in the title race]

1042
01:01:18,335 --> 01:01:20,737
[X THE LEAGUE Champions]
There's room for only one team

1043
01:01:20,737 --> 01:01:22,105
at the top of the pyramid.

1044
01:01:22,105 --> 01:01:26,910
They've fought their way
through a fierce competition to stand here.

1045
01:01:26,910 --> 01:01:31,615
The sellers on all eight teams
have given it their all.

1046
01:01:31,615 --> 01:01:36,870
But only one team will reach the top today.

1047
01:01:40,190 --> 01:01:44,027
Let me introduce the presenters
who will announce our champion.

1048
01:01:44,027 --> 01:01:46,434
KT ENA CEO Kim Ho Sang

1049
01:01:46,434 --> 01:01:48,567
and Lalastation CEO Lee Cheol Ho.

1050
01:01:48,567 --> 01:01:49,800
Please welcome them with a round of applause.

1051
01:01:49,800 --> 01:01:51,268
[Kim Ho Sang, CEO of ENA]

1052
01:01:51,268 --> 01:01:52,803
[Lee Cheol Ho, CEO of Lalastation]

1053
01:01:55,439 --> 01:01:58,721
Hello, I'm Kim Ho Sang, CEO of KT ENA.

1054
01:01:59,509 --> 01:02:04,381
Thank you to everyone who worked so hard
through the final round.

1055
01:02:04,381 --> 01:02:09,186
Bringing the world's top sellers together
to compete in Korea

1056
01:02:09,186 --> 01:02:12,893
made this a truly meaningful program.

1057
01:02:12,893 --> 01:02:18,762
For ENA, combining commerce
and broadcasting is a new venture,

1058
01:02:18,762 --> 01:02:21,031
so we're excited and have high hopes for it.

1059
01:02:21,031 --> 01:02:24,067
Thank you for all your hard work
in making it to the final round.

1060
01:02:24,067 --> 01:02:25,936
Thank you.

1061
01:02:25,936 --> 01:02:29,968
Now, let's hear a few words
from CEO Lee Cheol Ho.

1062
01:02:29,968 --> 01:02:31,925
Please give him a round of applause.

1063
01:02:35,012 --> 01:02:39,783
Thank you so much for the opportunity
to stand here on this special occasion.

1064
01:02:39,783 --> 01:02:43,729
I hope this marks a new beginning,
rather than an end.

1065
01:02:44,388 --> 01:02:48,091
To the 40 or so top sellers from nine countries

1066
01:02:48,091 --> 01:02:51,795
and the team owners
representing all nine countries,

1067
01:02:51,795 --> 01:02:53,397
congratulations once again,

1068
01:02:53,397 --> 01:02:57,167
and thank you sincerely
for helping us get this far.

1069
01:02:57,167 --> 01:02:58,235
Thank you.

1070
01:02:58,235 --> 01:03:00,237
Thank you.

1071
01:03:00,237 --> 01:03:05,142
Now, Kim Ho Sang is holding

1072
01:03:05,142 --> 01:03:07,411
the name of our winning team.

1073
01:03:07,411 --> 01:03:09,813
[Team Korea competes with strategy every round]

1074
01:03:11,267 --> 01:03:12,834
Today, with Noh Hee Young...

1075
01:03:12,834 --> 01:03:14,501
How does it look from a man's perspective?

1076
01:03:14,501 --> 01:03:17,554
Sangeununnie invited me here to model.

1077
01:03:17,554 --> 01:03:19,456
She's all muscle.

1078
01:03:19,456 --> 01:03:21,367
[Chasing a comeback to the very end]

1079
01:03:21,367 --> 01:03:24,701
[Team Indonesia dominates in total sales]

1080
01:03:24,701 --> 01:03:27,620
First place goes to Indonesia.

1081
01:03:28,367 --> 01:03:29,700
It's Indonesia.

1082
01:03:29,700 --> 01:03:31,868
[Unchallenged No. 1 in sales across all rounds]

1083
01:03:32,336 --> 01:03:35,405
[Team Indonesia consistently
ranks near the top]

1084
01:03:36,267 --> 01:03:41,081
[Korea vs. Indonesia]

1085
01:03:41,081 --> 01:03:42,179
Please announce the winner.

1086
01:03:42,179 --> 01:03:43,380
[The culmination of a 100-day journey]

1087
01:03:44,781 --> 01:03:48,051
X THE LEAGUE The Final Celebration.

1088
01:03:48,051 --> 01:03:49,356
[Which country will be crowned champion?]

1089
01:03:49,356 --> 01:03:51,510
The X THE LEAGUE champion.

1090
01:03:55,692 --> 01:04:00,130
[Who will claim
the glory after a fierce battle?]

1091
01:04:01,998 --> 01:04:04,836
Congratulations to Team Indonesia.

1092
01:04:04,836 --> 01:04:07,871
Our winner is Team Indonesia.

1093
01:04:07,871 --> 01:04:09,339
[Team Indonesia wins the championship]

1094
01:04:10,807 --> 01:04:15,545
Hur Young Soon, Ashanty, Ibnu,
Mami, Aurel, and Atta.

1095
01:04:15,545 --> 01:04:18,067
Congratulations to Team Indonesia.

1096
01:04:18,067 --> 01:04:19,116
Congratulations.

1097
01:04:19,116 --> 01:04:23,320
The winner of X THE LEAGUE Season 1
is Team Indonesia.

1098
01:04:23,320 --> 01:04:29,826
Team Indonesia has won
this 100-day sales battle.

1099
01:04:29,826 --> 01:04:33,530
Team Indonesia placed first in Round 5,

1100
01:04:33,530 --> 01:04:35,465
finishing with 47 points

1101
01:04:35,465 --> 01:04:39,803
and total sales of an incredible
20.2 billion won across all rounds

1102
01:04:39,803 --> 01:04:42,400
to become the first-ever X THE LEAGUE champion.

1103
01:04:42,400 --> 01:04:46,176
They're receiving the $500,000 prize.

1104
01:04:46,176 --> 01:04:49,446
They're also receiving bouquets.

1105
01:04:49,446 --> 01:04:52,082
And the trophy.

1106
01:04:52,082 --> 01:04:54,518
[Hard work earns the ultimate reward]

1107
01:04:54,518 --> 01:04:56,052
Incredible.

1108
01:04:56,052 --> 01:05:00,143
Every team member is also receiving a medal.

1109
01:05:02,025 --> 01:05:09,042
Team Indonesia has claimed
the first-ever X THE LEAGUE crown.

1110
01:05:09,934 --> 01:05:11,643
Congratulations.

1111
01:05:15,806 --> 01:05:19,268
Let's hear their acceptance speech.

1112
01:05:20,347 --> 01:05:21,971
Hello, everyone.

1113
01:05:22,634 --> 01:05:26,073
Thank you to everyone at X THE LEAGUE

1114
01:05:27,284 --> 01:05:32,193
for giving us the opportunity to compete.

1115
01:05:32,193 --> 01:05:35,992
Thank you to all the sellers
from every country who took part.

1116
01:05:35,992 --> 01:05:41,097
You're all amazing,
and I'm so happy to have met you.

1117
01:05:41,097 --> 01:05:46,770
And thank you to my husband, my children,
and my granddaughters.

1118
01:05:46,770 --> 01:05:48,968
To the best team in the world,

1119
01:05:48,968 --> 01:05:53,367
Atta, Aurel, Ibnu, and Mami,

1120
01:05:53,367 --> 01:05:56,964
and our amazing team owner, Ayu, thank you.

1121
01:06:00,067 --> 01:06:05,322
Finally, a heartfelt thank-you
to our fans, followers,

1122
01:06:05,322 --> 01:06:10,868
and everyone in Indonesia who supported us.

1123
01:06:10,868 --> 01:06:12,921
I love you. Bye.

1124
01:06:15,200 --> 01:06:16,833
Our first-ever X THE LEAGUE champion,

1125
01:06:17,634 --> 01:06:19,569
Team Indonesia.

1126
01:06:19,569 --> 01:06:23,840
[Celebrating their victory with every move]

1127
01:06:23,840 --> 01:06:28,278
Team Korea,
who fought for the title until the very end,

1128
01:06:28,278 --> 01:06:30,881
placed second in Round 5,

1129
01:06:30,881 --> 01:06:33,283
finishing second overall with 38 points

1130
01:06:33,283 --> 01:06:36,419
and total sales
of approximately 7.8 billion won

1131
01:06:36,419 --> 01:06:38,588
across all rounds.

1132
01:06:38,588 --> 01:06:41,525
We've shared this glorious moment together.

1133
01:06:41,525 --> 01:06:44,968
To all the sellers
from every country who competed so fiercely,

1134
01:06:44,968 --> 01:06:46,396
thank you for your hard work.

1135
01:06:46,396 --> 01:06:50,774
Congratulations once again
to all of today's award winners.

1136
01:06:53,167 --> 01:06:56,540
The top sellers representing their countries
on the eight teams gathered here

1137
01:06:56,540 --> 01:07:00,010
will face off in a fierce sales battle
on X THE LEAGUE.

1138
01:07:00,010 --> 01:07:02,212
[A fierce 100-day sales battle]

1139
01:07:02,879 --> 01:07:05,415
What's happening to us?

1140
01:07:05,415 --> 01:07:08,868
[The joy of reaching their goals]

1141
01:07:08,868 --> 01:07:10,779
[Learning the value of being together]
We'll take all 100,000.

1142
01:07:10,779 --> 01:07:13,114
- Like a corporation...
- Best partnership.

1143
01:07:14,133 --> 01:07:17,594
[There were painful goodbyes]

1144
01:07:17,594 --> 01:07:18,767
[And joyful encounters on X THE LEAGUE]

1145
01:07:18,767 --> 01:07:20,697
Oh, my goodness.

1146
01:07:23,567 --> 01:07:27,504
[100 days made brighter together.
Cheering on every seller's next challenge]

1147
01:07:28,672 --> 01:07:31,641
Now it's really time to say goodbye.

1148
01:07:31,641 --> 01:07:34,678
We'd like to thank everyone here
and all the viewers

1149
01:07:34,678 --> 01:07:37,681
who joined us on this long journey

1150
01:07:37,681 --> 01:07:40,016
as we bring the show to a close.

1151
01:07:40,016 --> 01:07:43,390
Thank you all for your hard work. Thank you.

1152
01:07:43,390 --> 01:07:45,755
- I've been your host, BamBam.
- I've been Tiffany Young.

1153
01:07:45,755 --> 01:07:47,567
And I've been Cho Jung Sik. Thank you.

1154
01:07:47,567 --> 01:07:48,992
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1155
01:07:48,992 --> 01:07:53,263
[We'll remember your passion
and cheer you on toward a bright future]

1156
01:07:53,263 --> 01:07:55,234
Thank you.

1157
01:07:55,234 --> 01:07:57,079
Being a seller...

1158
01:07:58,301 --> 01:08:02,405
may look easy, but it's really hard.

1159
01:08:02,405 --> 01:08:05,942
Standing out among so many sellers

1160
01:08:05,942 --> 01:08:07,911
isn't easy either.

1161
01:08:07,911 --> 01:08:11,581
I think I've found the answer

1162
01:08:11,581 --> 01:08:15,285
to what kind of person I need to be

1163
01:08:15,285 --> 01:08:17,187
to last in this business.

1164
01:08:17,187 --> 01:08:19,589
It was a meaningful experience.

1165
01:08:19,589 --> 01:08:24,160
I feel like I've caught a glimpse
of the path ahead.

1166
01:08:24,160 --> 01:08:25,996
[A meaningful experience,
a clearer path ahead]

1167
01:08:25,996 --> 01:08:31,501
I wanted to find brands and products I loved
and genuinely recommend them to my viewers.

1168
01:08:31,501 --> 01:08:32,669
My wife felt the same way.

1169
01:08:32,669 --> 01:08:36,039
Those shared feelings brought us
to this moment.

1170
01:08:36,039 --> 01:08:38,541
Just being able to share great brands
and products with people we care about

1171
01:08:38,541 --> 01:08:41,044
makes us happy and grateful every day.

1172
01:08:41,044 --> 01:08:44,147
Learning from people from so many countries
and seeing their passion

1173
01:08:44,147 --> 01:08:47,484
inspired me to dream of becoming

1174
01:08:47,484 --> 01:08:51,721
the best in Japan's emerging e-commerce market.

1175
01:08:51,721 --> 01:08:54,090
I want to learn from each country's strengths

1176
01:08:54,090 --> 01:08:56,926
and become Japan's top seller.

1177
01:08:56,926 --> 01:08:59,400
I really love livestream commerce.

1178
01:08:59,400 --> 01:09:05,101
I don't think it's just about selling things.

1179
01:09:05,101 --> 01:09:08,869
It's something I genuinely love
and feel passionate about.

1180
01:09:08,869 --> 01:09:11,741
Ultimately, I think passion matters most.

1181
01:09:11,741 --> 01:09:16,946
You have to truly love this work
to keep doing it.

1182
01:09:19,033 --> 01:09:20,850
[Our heartfelt thanks to all the sellers]

1183
01:09:20,850 --> 01:09:24,287
[And viewers who joined us
on this incredible journey]
